  m_text: 'Across

    2. _____ and aspart are the only rapid-acting insulin analogs
    currently classified as pregnancy risk Category B.

    4. An intermediate acting
    insulin with other of 2-5h and duration of 4-12h

    5. The fast-acting insulin
    that comes in a purple pre-filled pen that can be drawn into a syringe and mixed
    with NPH

    6. The fast-acting insulin that is found in Novomix

    8. Dose-dependent
    onset of action of 1-2h and duration of action of more than 12h. It can be given
    twice daily.'
